Hot Work Permit. For hot work that may occur on or near the Process, Kiva has developed a written Hot Work Permit program and procedure to document the requirements to complete the work and provide adequate fire prevention and process protection. 
With regard to hot work that may occur on or near the propane process, the Bakersfield Terminal has developed a written contractor evaluation program and a Hot Work Permit program to document the evaluation of the fire prevention and protection requirements. The Hot Work Permit system is implemented prior to allowing activities that could result in the generation of sparks (e.g. cutting and grinding) or that involve the use of open flames.
~~~~~
Contractor Safety. The Terminal uses contractors during periods of increased maintenance or construction activities. The Terminal evaluates and qualifies contractors who will work on the systems and equipment. Bakersfield Terminal has procedures in place to ensure that contractors  
	perform their work in a safe manner; 
	have appropriate knowledge and skills; 
	are aware of the hazards of their workplace; 
	understand what they should do in the event of an emergency; 
	understand and follow site specific safety rules; and  
	inform plan personnel of any hazards that they find while performing their work. 

Effective implementation of the contractor safety program is accomplished by providing contractors with an orientation session that covers (1) a process overview, (2) information about the safety and health hazards, (3) emergency response plan requirements and (4) safe work practices
